# stackcone Blog posts

When the user asks for a **blog post**, **guide**, or **how-to**, produce a published HTML article in `blog/posts/` and keep markdown source in `blog/md/`. Same visual system as `solutions/` (charts, Mermaid, tables, FAQ/HowTo JSON-LD). See `.cursor/rules/solution-posts.mdc` for shared HTML patterns (diagrams, pipeline, impl phases, chart.js).

## Source vs published (required)

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `blog/md/{slug}.md` | Authoring source — **not** a public URL |
| `blog/posts/{slug}.html` | Published page — canonical, sitemap, internal links |

- **Never** place `.md` files in `blog/posts/`.
- **Never** link to `.md` from HTML, `posts.json`, sitemap, or nav.
- `robots.txt` disallows `/blog/md/` — do not override with indexable links.
- Markdown sources and `_dev/` scripts are **removed before GitHub Pages deploy** (see `.github/scripts/prepare-pages.sh`); only `.html` is public.

## Deliverables (always)

1. `blog/md/{slug}.md` — markdown source (mirror of content)
2. `blog/posts/{slug}.html` — published page
3. Update `blog/posts.json` — add entry with `"author": "Amar Kumar"`
4. Update `sitemap.xml` — add `<url>` for the HTML page only
5. Run `python3 _dev/apply_highlights.py` on new/edited HTML (syntax highlighting)

**Slug:** lowercase, hyphenated (e.g. `how-sse-streaming-works-chatbots-llm-tokens`).

## posts.json entry

```json
{
  "id": "{slug}",
  "title": "Short outcome-focused title (no parenthetical subtitles)",
  "description": "Value + keywords in one sentence (under ~155 chars)",
  "href": "./posts/{slug}.html",
  "date": "YYYY-MM-DD",
  "dateLabel": "Month YYYY",
  "author": "Amar Kumar",
  "category": "RAG | Data | API | Docs | Freelancing | Platform",
  "tags": ["3–6 tags"]
}
```

## Article structure

- Opening hook — problem or misconception, then what the reader will learn
- Table of contents with anchor links
- H2 sections; code blocks and comparison tables where useful
- FAQ section + `FAQPage` JSON-LD when appropriate
- Related guides — link to other **`.html`** posts only
- CTA block at bottom (contact / solutions)

## SEO

Follow `.cursor/rules/seo-google.mdc`. Unique title, meta description, canonical (`https://stackcone.com/blog/posts/{slug}.html`), OG/Twitter, `Article` + `BreadcrumbList` JSON-LD.

## Tone

- Practical how-to or explainer — not a sales pitch
- Past tense OK for real experience; avoid fake metrics
- Upwork/freelance topics: actionable advice, not job-board provenance labels

## Syntax highlighting (required for code blocks)

Blog code uses **static span classes** in published HTML — same style as `blog/posts/how-to-build-a-production-rag-chatbot.html`. **Do not** use highlight.js, Prism, hljs CDN, or client-side highlighters.

### Token classes (`blog/blog.css`)

| Class | Use |
|-------|-----|
| `kw` | Keywords (`import`, `def`, `if`, `return`, `async`, …) |
| `fn` | Function names, builtins, types (`Path`, `len`, `str`, `embed`, …) |
| `str` | String literals (`"..."`, `'...'`, `f"..."`) |
| `num` | Numeric literals |
| `cm` | Comments (`# …`, `// …`) |

Pre blocks use dark background `#1e1e2e` (Catppuccin-style) — defined in `blog/blog.css`. No extra CSS or JS per post.

### Authoring workflow

1. **`blog/md/{slug}.md`** — write fenced code blocks normally (` ```python `, ` ```bash `, ` ```json `). Markdown source stays plain; no spans in `.md`.
2. **`blog/posts/{slug}.html`** — paste code inside `<pre><code>…</code></pre>` as **plain text** (escape `<` as `&lt;`, `&` as `&amp;` only where needed).
3. **Run the highlighter** before commit:

```bash
python3 _dev/apply_highlights.py
```

This scans `blog/posts/*.html`, wraps tokens in spans, and strips any stray `language-*` / highlight.js artifacts. Blocks that **already** contain `<span class="` are left unchanged.

4. Optional — highlight one file or re-run after edits:

```bash
python3 _dev/apply_highlights.py blog/posts/{slug}.html
```

### HTML shape (after `apply_highlights.py`)

```html
<pre><code><span class="kw">from</span> pathlib <span class="kw">import</span> <span class="fn">Path</span>

<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">chunk_text</span>(text: <span class="fn">str</span>) -&gt; <span class="fn">list</span>[<span class="fn">dict</span>]:
    <span class="kw">return</span> []</code></pre>
```

### Language detection (automatic)

`_dev/highlight_code.py` infers language from content when no hint exists:

| Detected | Heuristic |
|----------|-----------|
| Python | `import` / `def` / shebang |
| Bash | `python3`, `curl`, `grep`, `ls`, `mkdocs`, `#` comments |
| JSON | starts with `{` or `[` |
| JavaScript | `function`, `const`, `async` |
| SQL | `SELECT`, `FROM`, `JOIN`, `WHERE`, `GROUP BY` |
| YAML | `name:`, `on:`, `jobs:` at line start |
| Markdown | `---` frontmatter, `#` / `##` headings, `` `inline` `` code |
| Text | directory trees, `.env` samples — comments only |

Optional hint (stripped after run): `<pre><code class="language-python">` — prefer plain `<pre><code>` + `apply_highlights.py`.

### Do not

- Hand-wrap every token manually in long scripts (use `apply_highlights.py`)
- Add highlight.js / Prism CDN or `code-highlight.js` to post HTML
- Use `class="hljs"` or `language-*` as the final published form (runner removes hints)
- Put syntax-highlighted code only in `.md` and expect it on the live page without updating `.html`

### Shared tooling (do not duplicate per post)

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `_dev/highlight_code.py` | Span highlighter (python, bash, json, js, sql, yaml, md, text) |
| `_dev/apply_highlights.py` | Batch-apply to `blog/posts/*.html` |
| `blog/blog.css` | `.blog-article .kw` / `.fn` / `.str` / `.num` / `.cm` colors |

When adding or editing code in a blog post, **always run `apply_highlights.py`** on affected HTML before finishing.
